Riseonly patch on zed 6b2aa1c (Apache-2.0 crate gpui_macos), applied by scripts/vendor-gpui.py.
BGRA surface with alpha on macOS (P148): the Metal renderer drew a PaintSurface only from a full-range
biplanar YCbCr (420f) CVPixelBuffer and asserted on any other format. A kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA
buffer (premultiplied alpha, IOSurface backed) is now bound as one BGRA8Unorm texture from the
CVMetalTextureCache and drawn by bgra_surface_fragment with the path sprite blending (One,
OneMinusSourceAlpha), so a WebM sticker blends over the bubble and the chat background. The 420f
path is unchanged; any third format still asserts.

